---
title: "Subsurface travel"
note: "Codie's alien operator: something travels under the skin of HOST and surfaces at the end of its path. Every binding is a dial: route, skin, motion and reveal roll from the bh_ libraries, so ratings learn which mechanics H3 does best. HOST is your ref image 1; delete (image 1) for text only."
tags: [effects, h3, body_horror, ito]
---
@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic body horror, photorealistic
$host = __bh_host__
$entity = __bh_entity__
$route = __bh_route__
$surface = __bh_surface__
$motion = __bh_motion__
$reveal = __bh_reveal__

CAST
HOST (image 1): $host
ENTITY: $entity

SHOT 10s | push in, slow
HOST stands facing the camera, framed from the waist up, and at first appears completely normal. A localized pressure begins beneath the skin as ENTITY starts moving inside HOST, travelling $route. Throughout the movement HOST keeps $surface, and ENTITY is perceived only as a three-dimensional shape pressing outward from within. The movement stays $motion, and the areas it has already passed slowly return to their original form. In the final phase ENTITY reaches the end of its path and $reveal.
SFX: restrained breathing; subtle internal shifting; soft surface tension following the moving shape
MUSIC: N/A
